@@ -0,0 +1,44 @@
+---
+id: dl-004-importtasks-takes-an-optional-now-defaulting-to-the-wall-clock-outside-src-domain
+type: decision-log
+title: "importTasks takes an optional now, defaulting to the wall clock outside src/domain"
+status: approved
+---
+
+## Context
+
+The request asks for `importTasks(list, text)`, a bulk-import helper exported from `src/index.ts` that
+calls `list.add` once per non-blank line. `list.add` requires a `now`, per `dl-002`: `TaskList`'s
+mutating methods take `now` as a parameter rather than reading the clock themselves, because
+`r3-no-clock-or-randomness` forbids reading the clock under `src/domain/`. `importTasks` itself sits
+outside `src/domain/` (in a new `src/importTasks.ts`, re-exported from `src/index.ts`), the same place
+`dl-002` already names as free to read the real clock on behalf of the domain. The two-argument
+signature in the request leaves no obvious place for a caller to supply `now` explicitly, and the
+`testing` directive asks for deterministic tests, including for this helper.
+
+## Decision
+
+`importTasks(list, text, now = new Date().toISOString())`: a third, optional parameter. Calling it as
+`importTasks(list, text)` — the signature asked for — reads the real wall clock once per call and
+stamps every task imported by that call with the same `now`, consistent with `list.add` treating `now`
+as a single point in time per call. Tests (and any other caller that wants a fixed time) pass `now`
+explicitly instead of relying on the default.
+
+Parsing rejects a line that does not split into exactly 3 `;`-separated fields with a fixed reason of
+its own. For a line that does split into 3 fields, the parsed `title`/`priority`/`tags` are passed
+straight to `list.add`, and its `Result` error message (for an invalid title, an unknown priority, a
+duplicate title — tags built from whitespace-split fields cannot fail `validateTag`) becomes the
+`reason` reported for that line, rather than re-implementing those checks in `src/importTasks.ts`.
+
+## Consequences
+
+- `importTasks` can read the real clock, but only outside `src/domain/`, the same boundary `dl-002`
+  already draws; `src/domain/` stays exactly as constrained as before.
+- A caller matching the exact request (`importTasks(list, text)`) is unaffected; the new parameter is
+  additive and optional.
+- Validation wording for a rejected line (other than the "wrong number of fields" case) comes from
+  `src/domain/validation.ts` via `list.add`'s error message, so a future change to that wording changes
+  `importTasks`'s rejection reasons too — intentional, per `dl-003`'s single-source-of-validation goal.
+- As with `now` elsewhere (`dl-002`), nothing here checks that an explicitly passed `now` is a
+  well-formed ISO-8601 string.
+</content>
