@@ -0,0 +1,37 @@
+---
+id: task-004-add-importtasks-bulk-import-helper-to-src-index.ts
+type: task
+title: "Add importTasks bulk-import helper to src/index.ts"
+status: approved
+---
+
+## Request
+
+Teams migrating from spreadsheets need to bulk-import tasks. Add a public helper
+`importTasks(list, text)`, exported from `src/index.ts`, where `text` holds one task per line as
+`title;priority;tags` (priority may be empty for `normal`; tags are space-separated; blank lines are
+skipped). It adds every valid line to `list` and returns `{ imported, rejected }`, where `rejected`
+lists every line that could not be added as `{ line, reason }`, `line` counting from 1.
+
+## What was done
+
+- Added `src/importTasks.ts`, exporting `importTasks(list, text, now?)` and the `ImportResult` /
+  `RejectedLine` types. It is not under `src/domain/` because it reads the wall clock (via a defaulted
+  `now` parameter) when the caller does not supply one, which `r3-no-clock-or-randomness` forbids inside
+  `src/domain/`.
+- `src/index.ts` now re-exports `importTasks`, `ImportResult` and `RejectedLine`.
+- Parsing splits `text` on lines, skips blank ones (not counted as imported or rejected, but line
+  numbers still count them), and requires each non-blank line to split into exactly 3 `;`-separated
+  fields; a line that does not is rejected with a fixed reason rather than reaching `list.add`.
+- Field-level validation (empty/too-long title, unknown priority, tag with a space, duplicate title) is
+  not duplicated here: the parsed `title`/`priority`/`tags` are handed to `list.add`, and a rejection's
+  `reason` is `list.add`'s own `Result` error message, keeping validation in one place per `dl-003`.
+- Added `test/importTasks.test.ts`: a happy path (mixed priorities/tags/blank lines), a path covering a
+  malformed line, an invalid priority, and a duplicate title (checking exact line numbers and reasons),
+  and a test that the default `now` produces a well-formed ISO-8601 timestamp without asserting an exact
+  value (keeping the test deterministic per the `testing` directive).
+- `npm test` passes (23/23).
+
+## Follow-ups / risks
+
+- See decision-log `dl-004` for the `now` parameter and clock-reading placement.
